# ~birdbrain-deploy/.ssh/authorized_keys  (owner root, mode 0644; ~/.ssh owner root, mode 0755:
# the deploy user must not be able to edit its own restrictions; sshd StrictModes accepts root ownership)
# One line. "restrict" disables port/agent/X11 forwarding and the pty on modern OpenSSH;
# the explicit options are repeated for clarity and for older servers. The forced command
# ignores whatever the client asks to run, so this key can only trigger a deploy.
restrict,command="sudo /usr/local/sbin/birdbrain-deploy.sh",no-port-forwarding,no-agent-forwarding,no-X11-forwarding,no-pty ssh-ed25519 AAAA...REPLACE_WITH_THE_CI_PUBLIC_KEY... birdbrain-deploy@github-actions
